WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Those of you who are young students,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
this sacred duty is, in truth,
morally placed on your shoulders:

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.000
to understand what democracy is, and to build
a democratic system suited to Bangladesh,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.500
to build a democratic environment
suited to Bangladesh.

NOTE paragraph

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.000
So, first of all, let us understand what democracy is.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.100
I will not go into the debates of philosophers,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.500
because philosophers see politics
from one point of view,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:46.500
and politicians see politics
from another point of view.

NOTE paragraph

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:53.200
Let me come to Abraham Lincoln's famous definition.
Don't you know it? What is the definition of democracy? Who can tell me?

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.000
What did Abraham Lincoln say about democracy?

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.600
By the people, of the people, for the people, right?

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.000
By the people, for the people, and of the people.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Isn't it? This is the most effective definition of democracy.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.600
But in our Bangladesh, does this definition work?
